 "recipe": "one dial in, one dial out -- stellarator_helias\n\n0. read the input file   [167 nodes]\n      why    PROCESS's own question, verbatim -- the baseline both curves start from\n      op     (no graph operation)\n      note   8 chosen (8 `ixc`), 2 equalities and 12 inequalities, minimising\n             ^cond.numerics.objf; `values` is PROCESS's own converged answer\n1. make hfact a given   [167 nodes]\n      why    nobody picks the confinement factor: it is what the plasma does, so it is handed to us, not chosen\n      op     (no graph operation)\n      note   .physics.hfact leaves `chosen`, and PROCESS's own iteration variable 10 with it.\n      REFUSED NodePath(.Close.c2) holds (VarPath(^cond.constraints.c2),) against nothing: it has\n              no unknowns, so no driver can move it -- `Determine` it by a variable on its\n              cycle, or drop it\n2. the density absorbs the power balance   [168 nodes]\n      why    an ignited plasma is heated by its own alphas: at the operating temperature it sits at whatever density balances its losses\n      op     Insert(RootFind((^cond.constraints.c2,), (.physics.nd_plasma_electrons_vol_avg,))) at .Close.c2\n      op     nested_inside(.Close.c2)\n      note   the cycle it opens: 23 nodes (the other candidates, cheapest first:\n             .physics.f_nd_alpha_thermal_electron 20, .physics.b_plasma_toroidal_on_axis 25,\n             .physics.rmajor 25). .physics.nd_plasma_electrons_vol_avg leaves `chosen` -- it is\n             no longer ours\n3. freeze the build   [174 nodes]\n      why    the machine exists: its coils are wound, and nothing re-sizes them\n      op     Cut(.costs.life_div_fpy, 2 readers, ^built)\n      op     Insert(.Built.life_div_fpy)\n      op     Cut(.fwbs.life_blkt_fpy, 2 readers, ^built)\n      op     Insert(.Built.life_blkt_fpy)\n      op     Cut(.fwbs.life_fw_fpy, 1 readers, ^built)\n      op     Insert(.Built.life_fw_fpy)\n      op     Cut(.heat_transport.n_primary_heat_exchangers, 1 readers, ^built)\n      op     Insert(.Built.n_primary_heat_exchangers)\n      op     Cut(.vacuum.dia_vv_vacuum_ducts, 1 readers, ^built)\n      op     Insert(.Built.dia_vv_vacuum_ducts)\n      op     Cut(.vacuum.n_vac_pumps_high, 1 readers, ^built)\n      op     Insert(.Built.n_vac_pumps_high)\n      note   6 design variables held at PROCESS's answer; 6 build outputs were still being re-\n             sized by the dial and are now cut and checked (.costs.life_div_fpy,\n             .fwbs.life_blkt_fpy, .fwbs.life_fw_fpy, .heat_transport.n_primary_heat_exchangers,\n             .vacuum.dia_vv_vacuum_ducts, .vacuum.n_vac_pumps_high). Of the 13 conditions, 6 are\n             constants given the build (c82, c83, c32, c34, c35, c65) and 7 still depend on the\n             dial (c16, c24, c8, c17, c18, c67, c62)\n\n   chosen     (nothing: the machine is built)\n   conditions ^cond.constraints.c16, ^cond.constraints.c24, ^cond.constraints.c8,\n              ^cond.constraints.c17, ^cond.constraints.c18, ^cond.constraints.c67,\n              ^cond.constraints.c82, ^cond.constraints.c83, ^cond.constraints.c62,\n              ^cond.constraints.c32, ^cond.constraints.c34, ^cond.constraints.c35,\n              ^cond.constraints.c65, ^cond.built.costs.life_div_fpy,\n              ^cond.built.fwbs.life_blkt_fpy, ^cond.built.fwbs.life_fw_fpy,\n              ^cond.built.heat_transport.n_primary_heat_exchangers,\n              ^cond.built.vacuum.dia_vv_vacuum_ducts, ^cond.built.vacuum.n_vac_pumps_high",
